  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "wh-questions: where/what with be",
      "title_form": "Preguntas con where y what + be",
      "title_target": "Questions with where and what + be",
      "description_md_form": "Para preguntar por **lugar** o **información**, usamos **where** (dónde) y **what** (qué) con el verbo **be**.\n\n**Estructura:** *Wh-word + be + sujeto + ...?*\n\n- **Where** + *is* + sujeto → *Where is your friend?* (¿Dónde está tu amigo?)\n- **What** + *is* + sujeto → *What is your name?* (¿Cuál es tu nombre?)\n\nCon **you**, usamos **are**: *Where are you from?* (¿De dónde eres?).\n\nLa respuesta corta con **from** usa **I'm from + país**: *I'm from Spain.* (Soy de España).",
      "description_md_target": "To ask about **place** or **information**, we use **where** (dónde) and **what** (qué) with the verb **be**.\n\n**Structure:** *Wh-word + be + subject + ...?*\n\n- **Where** + *is* + subject → *Where is your friend?*\n- **What** + *is* + subject → *What is your name?*\n\nWith **you**, we use **are**: *Where are you from?*\n\nThe short answer with **from** uses **I'm from + country**: *I'm from Spain.*",
      "grammar_structure": "Wh-word + be + subject + ...?",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "present_simple_be",
        "headers": [
          "Pronombre",
          "Forma de be",
          "Ejemplo"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "I",
            "am",
            "I am from Spain."
          ],
          [
            "you",
            "are",
            "Where are you from?"
          ],
          [
            "he/she/it",
            "is",
            "Where is your friend?"
          ],
          [
            "we",
            "are",
            "We are from Mexico."
          ],
          [
            "they",
            "are",
            "They are students."
          ]
        ]
      },
